1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,580
 (upbeat music)

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:09,840
 Physical AI represents the next phase of AI adoption,

3
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:13,520
 building on the advances of generative AI and agentic AI,

4
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:17,320
 and extending intelligence beyond the digital world.

5
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:20,680
 Physical AI makes a shift from retrospective insight

6
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:23,880
 to intelligence embedded directly into the systems

7
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,680
 that drive the physical world.

8
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:30,080
 These systems sense, they decide, and act autonomously

9
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:33,280
 at speed, at scale, and in real time.

10
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:35,120
 Powering autonomous vehicles,

11
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:37,760
 highly automated factories and warehouses,

12
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:40,520
 self-monitoring and self-healing infrastructure,

13
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:44,520
 and intelligent medical device and industrial systems,

14
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:47,280
 physical AI turns intelligence into action

15
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:49,360
 and action into outcomes.

16
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:52,520
 (upbeat music)

17
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:55,280
 Industries are at a turning point.

18
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:58,440
 The real challenge is engineering intelligence

19
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:02,400
 that performs safely, reliably, and at scale

20
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:04,460
 amid the uncertainty of the real world

21
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:07,440
 where data is incomplete, conditions change,

22
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:10,240
 and decisions must be made in motion.

23
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:12,600
 Gartner identifies physical AI

24
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:15,440
 as the strategic technology trend expected

25
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:19,840
 to shape enterprise priorities over the next five years.

26
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:21,640
 Moving from pilots to production

27
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:23,440
 remains the defining hurdle.

28
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:26,920
 (upbeat music)

29
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:30,160
 Physical AI has to be embedded from the outset

30
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:33,800
 because once you move from pilots into live operations,

31
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:37,320
 constraints show up fast, such as latency, safety,

32
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:41,000
 and integration across hardware and enterprise systems.

33
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:44,200
 These are the challenges that models alone cannot solve.

34
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,320
 Complexity rises, costs escalate,

35
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:50,400
 and when systems lack transparency and explainability

36
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:53,200
 in real world conditions, confidence erodes,

37
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:56,200
 especially in regulated environments.

38
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,120
 That's why scaling breaks,

39
00:01:58,120 --> 00:01:59,880
 not because ambition is missing,

40
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:02,920
 but because the system was never designed to run,

41
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:05,440
 adapt, and stay safe in the real world.

42
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:12,160
 Physical AI must be architected across the full stack,

43
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:15,800
 integrating sensing, decision-making, actuation,

44
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,440
 data platforms, and enterprise systems

45
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:21,200
 into a single coherent design.

46
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:24,560
 That means validating performance through simulation

47
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:29,400
 before deployment, introducing capability in staged releases,

48
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:32,800
 and governing models continuously as they evolve.

49
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:36,240
 This is an architectural shift, not a feature upgrade,

50
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:38,840
 and it's not confined to one team.

51
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:43,560
 It requires clear ownership across IT, OT, engineering,

52
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:46,360
 and operations because physical AI

53
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,360
 doesn't live in a single function.

54
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:54,760
 We're already seeing this shift across industries

55
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:56,880
 as digital and physical intelligence

56
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:59,600
 converge in real-world systems.

57
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:02,960
 In manufacturing, AI is shifting operations

58
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:07,680
 from periodic inspection to continuous autonomous optimization.

59
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:10,360
 In mobility, software-defined vehicles

60
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:14,440
 are evolving safely over time through embedded intelligence.

61
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:18,680
 And in life sciences, simulation and human-in-the-loop validation

62
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:21,400
 are accelerating innovation while protecting

63
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,240
 safety and regulatory trust.

64
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:31,000
 At Cognizant, we engineer physical AI across the full lifecycle,

65
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,040
 from simulation and validation through to deployment

66
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:36,560
 in complex, regulated environments,

67
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:39,680
 building intelligent, connected systems designed

68
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:42,840
 for autonomous operation in the real world.

69
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:46,120
 That's why we continue to invest in our global innovation

70
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:49,960
 centers that allow our clients to design, test,

71
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:53,080
 and industrialize solutions before scaling them

72
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,440
 into live operations.

73
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:01,840
 The next phase of AI won't be defined by algorithms alone,

74
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:04,720
 but by how intelligently we engineer them

75
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:06,240
 into the real world.

76
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:08,240
 The organizations that succeed will

77
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:10,040
 be those that engineer intelligence

78
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:14,960
 with rigor, discipline, and responsibility from day one.

79
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:18,700
 (gentle music)

